  "answer": "Read only, no rule. Both reads agree in all 8 setups. A single phone edit on blocks fresh from desktop never changed the DOM order, in 7 of 7 setups (e1 to e7): move or resize, onto a block or apart, up or down, lower or higher z, 2 or 3 blocks. That holds even in e5, where a1 moved to phone row 10, below a2 on row 7, and the DOM kept a1 first. The second edit in e8 did change it: a2, already moved onto a1, was resized onto a3, and the DOM became z2, z1, z3 (a3 stayed last). Ours keeps the order everywhere except e5, where it puts z2 first. So ours misses e5 and e8's second edit. Not seen: a rule that fits these reads together with CAP-A2CORPUS1STEPS (there, z2's moves and resizes left the order alone until its resize into a chain gave z3, z2, z1)."
